            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-34428",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "jetty: SessionListener can prevent a session from being invalidated breaking logout"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "For Eclipse Jetty versions \u003c= 9.4.40, \u003c= 10.0.2, \u003c= 11.0.2, if an exception is thrown from the SessionListener#sessionDestroyed() method, then the session ID is not invalidated in the session ID manager. On deployments with clustered sessions and multiple contexts this can result in a session not being invalidated. This can result in an application used on a shared computer being left logged in."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2021-34428",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-34428\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-server\nFixed Version: 9.4.41, 10.0.3, 11.0.3\nLink: [CVE-2021-34428](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2021-34428)\nFor Eclipse Jetty versions \u003c= 9.4.40, \u003c= 10.0.2, \u003c= 11.0.2, if an exception is thrown from the SessionListener#sessionDestroyed() method, then the session ID is not invalidated in the session ID manager. On deployments with clustered sessions and multiple contexts this can result in a session not being invalidated. This can result in an application used on a shared computer being left logged in.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-34428**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-server|9.4.41, 10.0.3, 11.0.3|[CVE-2021-34428](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2021-34428)|\n\nFor Eclipse Jetty versions \u003c= 9.4.40, \u003c= 10.0.2, \u003c= 11.0.2, if an exception is thrown from the SessionListener#sessionDestroyed() method, then the session ID is not invalidated in the session ID manager. On deployments with clustered sessions and multiple contexts this can result in a session not being invalidated. This can result in an application used on a shared computer being left logged in."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 3.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:P/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
